# Lint after TypeScript changes

After you add or change any `.ts` or `.tsx` file, run lint on those files before finishing:

```bash
npx next lint --file <changed-file.ts>
```

If several files added and/or changed, pass each with `--file`. Use `npm run lint` when the change is broad (same check as Vercel `next build`).

If lint fails, fix the reported issues and re-run until it passes. Do not leave a red lint that would fail deploy.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — @typescript-eslint/prefer-nullish-coalescing
Boolean(env.BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN || process.env.VERCEL)

// ✅ GOOD
Boolean(env.BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN ?? process.env.VERCEL)
```
